{
 "id": "track-filter",
 "order": 12,
 "name": "Per Track LP Filter + Env Amt & Latched Filter Mode",
 "description": [
  "A 12 dB low-pass filter per track (or 24 dB, per track) with light saturation, resonance and its own decay envelope.",
  "Hold RETRIG + press GATE = filter mode on: PITCH = cutoff, DECAY = envelope decay, COLOR = resonance,",
  "SHAPE = envelope amount (bipolar, centre = off); the four knob LEDs light up. Tap RETRIG = off",
  "(turning a knob while RETRIG is held keeps the mode). Cutoff 127 = filter off.",
  "Hold GATE + press PLAY = filter reset of the selected track. GATE toggles on release.",
  "In the filter mode, FUNC + GATE = 12 dB / 24 dB for the selected track (saved per pattern, header byte 58).",
  "Four real parameters on every machine: p-lockable, LFO and velocity destinations, CC 74 / 71, saved with the sound."
 ],
 "device": "Model:Cycles OS 1.13 (also a Model:Samples running it)",
